  "worked_solution": "To solve the inequality $p(x)\\ge 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=p(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is \n$x\\in [-1,\\infty ).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/da89900d3087b93e20a63485b35af41097a2bf21a48f88a027b9afd3c1bb276c.png)",
